syntax: reset the assignment offset for every token

Parser.eqlOffs records where '=' sits in the current literal, and
hasValidIdent and getAssign index Parser.val with it. Only the lexer path
for unquoted words reset it, so a literal token produced on another path
kept the offset of an earlier word. With RecoverErrors, an arithmetic
expansion that fails to parse after an assignment reaches getAssign with
that stale offset and panics:

	NewParser(RecoverErrors(3)).Parse(strings.NewReader("v=$(( x  y ))"), "")
	panic: runtime error: slice bounds out of range [2:1]

The offset is now reset at the start of every token.

diff --git a/syntax/lexer.go b/syntax/lexer.go
index 72f850d..4586416 100644
--- a/syntax/lexer.go
+++ b/syntax/lexer.go
@@ -248,6 +248,7 @@ func (p *Parser) nextKeepSpaces() {
 }
 
 func (p *Parser) next() {
+	p.eqlOffs = -1
 	if p.r == runeEOF {
 		p.tok = _EOF
 		return
